   "args": {
    "summary": "Diagnosed and repaired the L2-1 failure of the three-span cast-in-place continuous box-girder bridge (35+45+35 m, cast_box h=2.2 m, C50 with Ec=37000 MPa override, spine-beam 2D, continuous_on_piers).\n\nRoot cause: the laminated-elastomeric bearing rubber layer thickness was present in the instance only as \"t1_mm\" (11 mm per the description). The JTG 3362-2018 8.7 clauses (shape factor S, vertical stiffness Kv, shear stiffness Kh) read a field named \"t1\" in metres; with neither \"t1\" present, the formula layer silently fell back to the 8 mm schema default, so the clause re-computation (S=20.19 vs 14.69, etc.) no longer matched the accepted bearing decisions — the three L2-1 \"model check failed\" entries with empty suspect lists. Fix: rewrote the bearing instances with the full bearing objects plus t1 = 0.011 m (keeping t1_mm = 11 mm per the description). This restored agreement between the instance and the code formulas (S, Kv, Kh now reproduce the accepted values exactly).\n\nExisting values were otherwise correct and unchanged: girder A=6.712 m², I=4.498 m⁴ (verified by section integration), w=174.512 kN/m, m=17.789 t/m; pier twin-column D=1.8 m, A=5.089 m², I=1.031 m⁴, Ec=32500 MPa (C40); bearings 2 per line on each of 4 support lines. Re-proposed the 20 invalidated bearing decisions and lane.mu (μ=0.1806, from f1=3.037 Hz via JTG D60-2015 4.3.2), re-ran the modal analysis, and regenerated the model successfully.\n\nKey results: vertical frequencies 3.037 / 4.653 / 5.398 Hz (f1=3.037 Hz); self-weight support reactions 2240.8, 7799.8, 7779.5, 2248.8 kN; self-weight midspan moments 12492.5, 15853.1, 12631.6 kNm and support moments −28459.2, −28181.2 kNm; Class I lane max positive moment 11474.2 kNm, max negative moment −9092.7 kNm."
